---
description: Enforce feature boundaries in UI components
globs:
  - "src/features/**/*.ts"
  - "src/features/**/*.tsx"
alwaysApply: false
---

## Feature boundaries

- Keep full domain models (`Booking`, `UserProfile`, `Course`, etc.) in containers, services, and domain workflows.
- Presentational components (cards, rows, cells, sections, dialogs) must receive a feature-specific `*Input` contract or prepared view model.
- Do not use `Pick<...>` from a broad context directly in a component declaration. Define the focused type in the feature’s contracts module instead.
- Pass IDs and narrow callbacks for open, delete, move, or select actions; resolve full entities in the container.
- Import domain models in feature contracts modules, not in new presentational child components.
- Use feature translation hooks such as `useStudentCabinetTranslations` or `useScheduleTranslations`; do not import `useLanguage()` directly in new child UI components.
- Keep calculations, sorting, filtering, and formatting out of JSX.
- Refactor legacy code only when touching that area or when coupling causes a concrete maintenance issue.